What type of graph does the equation produce? Name the family and give the general form of its equation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.2)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,smooth,domain=0.42:3,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1.3/\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,smooth,domain=-3:-0.42,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1.3/\x});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What type of graph does the equation produce? Name the family and give the general form of its equation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\draw[->] (-3.2,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6)--(0,3.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,smooth,domain=-2:2.6,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.8*exp(-\x*ln(2))});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

